 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Most families still split them down the middle between parents, then add a little for the couple if they' very generous. Then I'd lead with your parents' offer, and only top it up by a few hundred yourself. No point in making it sound like you' footing the whole bill. Not rude, just practical. Weddings are expensive enough without anyone having regrets about how much they contributed. Then maybe suggest a payment plan instead of turning it down outright. Most people do want help, they just might not realize it yet. Good plan. He'll appreciate the thought. Then you might want to lead with your parents' offer first, just to keep things balanced.",
